I left out the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, so it cannot write to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or call the metadata service. Those would need their own granted capabilities, such as an HTTP client handle for the enrichment fetch and a logging capability, or they belong in the host. I also assumed the node should mark items seen only when the digest was published.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;
use std::collections::BTreeSet;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        if published.published {
            let ids: BTreeSet<&str> = published.considered.iter().map(|s| s.as_str()).collect();
            for id in ids {
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
